  "unresolvedAiThreads": [
    {
      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDORKRjBc6eCimx",
      "replyToCommentDatabaseId": 3902539306,
      "path": "VAA.EAPI.Microservices/VAA.EAPI.Microservices.CRM.Email/README.md",
      "line": 20,
      "url": "https://github.com/VAAD1ST/eapi/pull/1731#discussion_r3902539306",
      "author": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer",
      "body": "This README says the under-18 confirmation email \"sends only\" three merge fields, but the Member Management event mapper also populates additional fields (e.g., `Customer_LastName`, `Membership_Number`, `Member_First_Name`). Reword this to avoid documenting a stricter contract than the code actually emits.",
      "decision": "valid",
      "resolutionComment": "Updated the CRM Email README to distinguish parent-only recipient routing from the full merge payload and to list all six fields populated by HouseHoldAccountEmailTriggeringEventMapper: Customer_FirstName, Customer_LastName, Membership_Number, Member_First_Name, Child_First_Name, and Child_Membership_Number."
    },
    {
      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDORKRjBc6eCinc",
      "replyToCommentDatabaseId": 3902539368,
      "path": "VAA.EAPI.Microservices/VAA.EAPI.Microservices.CRM.Email/README.md",
      "line": 26,
      "url": "https://github.com/VAAD1ST/eapi/pull/1731#discussion_r3902539368",
      "author": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer",
      "body": "This paragraph states suppression is for the exact `U18.virgin.com` domain, but the dummy domain is treated as configurable (`DummyEmailDomain`) in the under-18 flow. Align the wording with the configurable domain (and keep `U18.virgin.com` as the default) so docs don't diverge from configuration-driven behaviour.",
      "decision": "invalid",
      "resolutionComment": "No change made. The shared EmailRecipientPolicy suppression boundary is intentionally implemented with the constant Under18DummyEmailDomain = U18.virgin.com and compares recipients to that exact domain. DummyEmailDomain config is used upstream by the Identity and Member Management under-18 flows; it does not configure CRM/CCP or Adobe/ACM delivery suppression, so the existing README accurately documents the delivery boundary."
    }
  ],
